This local speech denoiser does not identify the person the wearer wants to hear.
Removed sound can contain wanted speech; retained sound can contain other voices.
The fixed speech/residual bands are development-derived operational decisions,
not measured acoustic SNR or wearer intelligibility. They must agree with the
existing speech-masking head before the original fresh-check/cooldown policy.
No wearer training, enrollment or stored noise profile. No cleaned audio playback,
recordings, transcripts or network inference. Source audio is not packaged.

Fixed bands use the licensed development mixes credited in masking/sources.json.
No heldout examples or wearer data fit these bands.
